==============================================================================================================
VERDICT (W1-W4)
==============================================================================================================
  A swirled river pushes co-moving (prograde) and counter-moving (retrograde) bodies oppositely: that sign flip is the
  swirl's fingerprint.  GR's own swirl of the Milky Way's river (frame dragging, baryons only) is 0.0e+00 - 0.0e+00 of Newtonian gravity
  at 8-10 kpc (pushing co-rotating stars outward), a river turning at ~0.11 m/s, with local frames rotating at 0.0e+00 mas/yr; no galactic observable can see it.
  (First run: the prose here was hard-coded as 'about a millionth' and '~a metre per second', which overstated the printed
  numbers; it now prints them.  Checks and numbers are unchanged; see cfg179_s3_swirl_gr_firstrun.out.)

